      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Analysis of data obtained in the study of the blood enzymatic and isoenzymatic spectra (creatine phosphokinase and lactate dehydrogenase with simulatenous study of aspartate and alanine transaminases) in patients with various forms of ischemic heart disease showed the close correlation of the studied tests with the clinical picture of the disease, the degree and depth of myocardial involvement. The enzymatic tests studied are of diagnostic and prognostic importance and may be used in the differential diagnosis of various forms of ischemic heart disease."},
